{'symbol': 'EXC', 'date': '2021-07-19 10:00:00', 'title': "ILLINOIS' NUCLEAR PLANTS NEAR 41 YEARS OF PROVIDING SAFE, RELIABLE, CARBON-FREE POWER", 'text': "WARRENVILLE, ILL.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--AT A TIME WHEN THE NATION'S ENERGY GRID IS INCREASINGLY CHALLENGED BY EXTREME HEAT AND STORMS, THE FOUR NUCLEAR PLANTS SERVING CHICAGO AND NORTHERN ILLINOIS ARE APPROACHING A COMBINED 41 YEARS, OR 15,000 CONSECUTIVE DAYS, OF CONTINUOUS SERVICE. THE DRESDEN, BYRON, BRAIDWOOD AND LASALLE NUCLEAR PLANTS LOCATED OUTSIDE THE CHICAGO REGION PROVIDE MORE THAN TWO-THIRDS OF THE STATE'S CARBON-FREE ENERGY AND ARE THE ONLY CLEAN-ENERGY RESOURCES THAT CAN OPERATE AROUND"}